"""patch_prereg_addendum7_1030.py (2026-10-30): appends Addendum 7 (the procedure for earnings_role_bands_walk_forward, scripts/card/earnings_role_band_test.py)
to results/PREREG_g7_proven_rerun_2026-10-29.md. The registration must be exactly the version after Addendum 6 (sha256 1d86b4f9...) and the placeholder must occur
exactly once, or nothing is changed. No registered prediction is edited: the text before PRED-TABLE-END is compared before and after.
Usage: python3 scripts/audit/patch_prereg_addendum7_1030.py [results/PREREG_g7_proven_rerun_2026-10-29.md]"""
import hashlib, sys
def sha(s): return hashlib.sha256((s if s.endswith("\n") else s + "\n").encode("utf-8")).hexdigest()
p = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "results/PREREG_g7_proven_rerun_2026-10-29.md"
T = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()
assert sha(T) == "1d86b4f9f69970952f064219d6d7ef27d5e3bb380fde6fa4d24f31782c3a25aa", "the registration is not the version after Addendum 6; nothing changed"
old = "(further dated addenda go here: the remaining procedures)"
assert T.count(old) == 1, "placeholder not found exactly once; nothing changed"
new = """### Addendum 7 (2026-10-30, before the run): earnings_role_bands_walk_forward, scripts/card/earnings_role_band_test.py

**What the script does, read from its own text.** It is read-only and writes nothing to the database or the disk (console output only). From the earnings 8-K filings (item 2.02) of each stock it builds band units from the matrices, classifies each stock's earnings timing habit from its earlier quarters (before the open or after the close, from the overnight gap) and compares walk-forward 90% bands (pooled day i and day i+1; habit-assigned reaction day and other day; four groups; a placebo with shuffled habits) by interval score and by coverage, by era. Its pre-set rule, written on 2026-10-21 before the first run: ROLE BANDS IMPROVE if, in each of the three eras, the ROLES interval score is at least 2.0% below POOLED, ROLES coverage is within 88% to 92% on the reaction day and on the other day, and the PLACEBO ratio is at least 0.99. Usage: python3 -u scripts/card/earnings_role_band_test.py, no arguments; credentials from the environment. Original printout: results/2026-10-19/earnings_role_band_test.out (29 lines, 43 seconds), committed as fb841e3 at 2026-10-21 15:24:57, three minutes after the script's only commit 2f031f2 (15:21:44). The folder name 2026-10-19 does not match the commit date, but the three-minute gap shows that the printout belongs to this version of the script.

**Pin.** Commit 63e08d84, a state before commit b68b1b1 (2026-10-22), which refit the role model and changed day_card.py; the run prints the pin's own commit line. The script has one commit (2f031f2), so it is identical at the pin and at HEAD; event_width_test.py has one commit (ea2a09f, 2026-10-19), so it is identical at both as well; day_card.py, unrecorded_candidates.py and earnings_timing_check.py are taken as of the pin.

**Every input, checked on 2026-10-30 from git and the file system (the rule of Addendum 4a).**
1. Code: the script and its four imported modules, from the worktree at the pin. Their import-time statements were read: only constants (EXCLUDED_TYPES, ERAS, BASE_NEAR); nothing is read or written on import.
2. data_cache/audit_matrices.npz: 35,221,184 bytes, written 2026-10-20 14:16, sha256 7bd617a487a40d8949ecbad3cbb7481b9f1ae61df4b9eac76edb2255023963e6; keys E, SD, Y, dates, ids, tickers; 496 stocks by 8,250 days, 1994-01-03 to 2026-10-13. An untracked cache, supplied to the worktree by a symbolic link to the repository's data_cache; its hash is printed again before ARM 0 and must match.
3. data_cache/ohlc: 497 pickles, all written between 2026-10-21 14:16 and 14:25, which is before the original run (the script's commit is 15:21:44), and untouched since; supplied by the same link; not hashed (the count and the newest and oldest modification times are printed again before ARM 0).
4. Database tables, read over REST (SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_KEY are set): securities (id, entity_id); event_direction_labels (event_id, size, timing), read by event_width_test.load_event_info and unused by this script's result; ev_ent (event_id, entity_id, d, ptype), 22,338 rows, latest day 2026-09-11, which supplies the recorded event days (the event day and the next trading day); sec_8k_filings (security_id, filing_date, item_codes), 155,141 rows through 2026-09-18, 41,459 with item 2.02. ARM 1 also reads event_exclusions (event_id, severity).
5. Model files: none. Seven model files are tracked at the pin and will be present in the worktree, but nothing on this script's path reads them; models/earnings_role_band_model.json (first committed in b68b1b1) is not at the pin and is not needed.
6. Output: console only; each arm's console output is saved with tee under results/g7_rerun/.

**Latest dates compared with the original run (the rule of Addendum 2).** The matrices (2026-10-13) and the OHLC cache (2026-10-21) are unchanged since before the original run. sec_8k_filings has 155,141 rows through 2026-09-18, the same count the changelog recorded on 2026-10-21 after the original run. ev_ent has 22,338 rows with latest day 2026-09-11, so earnings filings after 2026-09-11 can carry no recorded-event flag in this re-run; whether the original run had the same window is tested by ARM 0.

**Set-up (the same commands will be run).** git worktree add /tmp/g7_pin_role 63e08d84 (its commit line is printed), then a symbolic link /tmp/g7_pin_role/data_cache to the repository's data_cache (refusing if one already exists). The worktree is removed afterwards.

**ARM 0** is the pinned script, unpatched. It must reproduce the original printout: after removing the two elapsed-time items (the last field of the first line and the line that starts with total) the output is identical line by line: 33,023 isolated earnings events from 2006, 29,737 with a forward habit (90.0%), a BMO share of 61.9%, every row of the results table, the three READING lines and the verdict. The PLACEBO rows are identical if the script seeds its random generator (the run prints the script's seed lines first); if it does not, they must be within 0.005 in each era and the placebo condition (at least 0.99) must hold. If any other line differs, the run STOPS and the cause (database drift in ev_ent, securities or sec_8k_filings since 2026-10-21, a cache, or the code) is found before ARM 1; the differences are then reported as the effect of that cause.

**ARM 1** is the same after scripts/audit/g7_patch_arm1_event_width_v2.py edits ONLY the worktree's copy of event_width_test.py: rows of ev_ent whose event_id has an exclude row in event_exclusions are skipped, so their days stop being recorded event days, and the number of skipped rows is printed. The patch used for the two earlier flags (g7_patch_arm1_event_width.py) counts the skipped rows but its printed text does not show the count and, as it appears in the 2026-10-30 session record, it does not stop a second application (tested on a copy: a second run inserts the filter again, which repeats the same filter and doubles the printed lines without changing a result); whether the committed copy differs is checked by the run block. v2 refuses a second application, a path outside /tmp and a target text that does not match exactly once, prints the skipped-row count, and was tested on a faithful copy of load_event_info (an excluded event is dropped; a row whose severity is note is kept).

**Tripwires.** (1) ARM 1 prints that 716 ev_ent rows were skipped, equal to the pre-check (716 of 22,338); any other number stops the run. (2) ARM 1 must not isolate FEWER earnings events than ARM 0; the same count is allowed only because tripwire 1 shows the filter acted (the 716 rows are mostly events with no price history, and the width test's own-event days fell by only 10 of 41,542 under the same filter). (3) The pinned worktree's git status must show only the one edited file in ARM 1 and nothing in ARM 0; each arm's output and the patch diff are saved to results/g7_rerun/ with the arm in the name.

**Stated in advance.** (a) The registered rows p11 to p14 describe ARM 1, as for the other event-level flags; ARM 0 is reported beside it. (b) ARM 1 is expected to be almost identical to ARM 0. (c) The thin margins of the original printout: the highest coverage cell is ROLES on other days in 2020-2026 at 91.9%, 0.1 below the 92% upper limit and printed to one decimal; the lowest is ROLES on reaction days in 2013-2019 at 88.5%, 0.5 above 88%. p13 prices only the lowest; a shift of 0.1 points upward in the highest cell would fail the registered rule although no coverage got worse. p14 stands as registered and is not edited; this margin is recorded here and not used to change it. (d) The limits stated in the script's own docstring are unchanged: the choice of the last 4 quarters came from the recency test on the same years, band units come from the same matrices the card uses, and a forward use needs the filing date known in advance. Nothing here re-scores or edits a prediction.

(further dated addenda go here: the remaining procedures)"""
head_before = T[:T.index("PRED-TABLE-END")]
R = T.replace(old, new)
assert R[:R.index("PRED-TABLE-END")] == head_before, "a registered prediction would change; nothing written"
open(p, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(R)
R2 = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read(); print("ok   Addendum 7 appended"); print("PREREG sha256", sha(R2), "|", R2.count("\n"), "lines")
